        "by": "greptile-apps",
        "outdated": false,
        "first_comment": "<a href=\"#\"><img alt=\"P1\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\"></a> **Forks Share Mutable Config**\n\nWhen project code has already imported `rxconfig`, a forked `RegistrationContext` receives that module's existing mutable `Config` object. This conflicts with `RegistrationContext.fork()`, which resets `_config` and promises that the next `get_config()` call reloads it. The parent and fork can therefore share configuration mutations, allowing persistent overrides or other changes from one app to leak into the other.\n\n**Knowledge Base Used:** [Application lifecycle and configuration](https://app.greptile.com/reflex-org-2/-/custom-context/knowledge-base/reflex-dev/reflex/-/docs/application-lifecycle.md)",
        "path": "packages/reflex-base/src/reflex_base/config.py",
        "line": 1103,
